body":"**Migrated issue, originally created by Luke Cyca ([@lukecyca](https://github.com/lukecyca))**\n\n\n    from sqlalchemy.ext.declarative import declarative_base\n    from sqlalchemy import *\n    from sqlalchemy.orm import *\n    Base = declarative_base()\n    \n    \n    class Document(Base):\n        __tablename__ = 'documents'\n    \n        id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True)\n    \n        @classmethod\n        def __declare_last__(cls):\n    \n            cls.result_type = column_property(\n                select([distinct(Result.type)](distinct(Result.type)))\n                .where(Result.document_id == cls.__table__.c.id)\n            )\n    \n    \n    class Result(Base):\n        __tablename__ = 'results'\n    \n        id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True)\n        type = Column(Unicode)\n        document_id = Column(Integer, ForeignKey(Document.id))\n        document = relationship(Document)\n    \n    \n    session = Session()\n    \n    # This works\n    print session.query(Document)\n    \n    # This does not\n    print session.query(Document).join(Result)\n\n\n\nI would like both of these queries to work. I would expect the latter to emit the following query:\n\n\n    SELECT\n        documents.id AS documents_id, \n        (\n            SELECT DISTINCT results.type\n            WHERE results.document_id = documents.id\n        ) AS anon_1 \n    FROM documents\n    JOIN results ON documents.id = results.document_id\n\n\nI've tried using various forms of select().correlate() and select().correclate_except() but I don't think there is any way to make both of the above queries work.\n\nI've verified this behaviour in the latest 0.8 snapshot as well as the 0.8.0b2 release.\n\n","closed_by":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","